   "source": [
    "Looking at the `describe()` results for `df3`, useful insights include the center, spread, and range of the numeric columns, along with the quartiles that help show how the values are distributed. These summaries are more useful when the columns represent meaningful measurements such as prices, quantities, or totals. Compared with the previous example, the summaries may be different because `df3` likely has different types of numeric columns and may include fewer ID-like fields. If a dataset contains mostly true measured values, `describe()` gives more useful business insight; if it contains many identifier columns, some of the summary statistics are less meaningful.\n"
   ]
